IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 1 -- Preliminary (ss 1 to 5).
-- s 1 (short title) and s 3 (repealed) have no rule here: the short title is machinery and s 3 is blank in the text.

§ `Part 1 -- Preliminary`

§§ `s 2 -- Act applies to all Acts`

-- "This Act applies to all Acts (including this Act)."  The section names the things it applies to and does not say that it applies
-- to nothing else, so a thing that is not an Act gets NOTHING.
-- src:15 | 2 Act applies to all Acts
-- src:16 | This Act applies to all Acts (including this Act).
@ref s 2 (src:15-16)
GIVEN `the thing is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies to the thing (s 2)` IS
    IF `the thing is an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- The Note to s 2 points to the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, part 4, divisions 1 and 2, which is not among the sources.
-- Whether that Act applies this Act to a statutory instrument is taken as an input.
-- src:17 | Note—
-- src:18 | For the application of this Act to statutory instruments, see the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, part 4, divisions 1 and 2.
@ref s 2 Note (src:17-18)
GIVEN `the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, part 4, divisions 1 and 2 apply this Act to the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies to a statutory instrument (s 2 Note)` IS
    IF `the Statutory Instruments Act 1992, part 4, divisions 1 and 2 apply this Act to the instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 4 -- Displacement of Act by contrary intention`

DECLARE `How far this Act's application is displaced` IS ONE OF
    `wholly`
    `partly`

-- "The application of this Act may be displaced, wholly or partly, by a contrary intention appearing in any Act."
-- With no contrary intention the section says nothing about displacement, so the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:21 | The application of this Act may be displaced, wholly or partly, by a contrary intention appearing in any Act.
@ref s 4 (src:21-21)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears in an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention reaches the whole of this Act's application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `How far this Act's application is displaced`
DECIDE `how far a contrary intention displaces this Act (s 4)` IS
    IF NOT `a contrary intention appears in an Act`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the contrary intention reaches the whole of this Act's application`
         THEN JUST `wholly`
         ELSE JUST `partly`

§§ `s 5 -- Act binds Crown`

-- "This Act binds the Crown."
-- src:23 | This Act binds the Crown.
@ref s 5 (src:23-23)
GIVEN `the person bound is the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act binds the person (s 5)` IS
    IF `the person bound is the Crown` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
